<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chlodwig zu Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1819–1901</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Chlodwig, Prince of Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chlodwig zu Hohenlohe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schillingsfurst">Schillingsfürst</a> (1819–1901) was a German statesman who served as prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 1866 to 1870, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace-lorraine">Alsace-Lorraine</a> from 1885 and Chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> and Prussian prime minister from 1894 to 1900. A liberal Catholic aristocrat, he backed German unification under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, but as chancellor he was largely overshadowed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chlodwig-zu-hohenlohe-schillingsfurst.jpg" alt="Chlodwig zu Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: various · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Die_Gartenlaube_(1894)_b_773_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
